  "review_notes": [
    "All1505B original and3149B organized bytes read separately, including all four whole records and complete genuine projection theorem.",
    "BitMatrixStreamMaterializer stores an actual pure function from a stream to a list of String pairs and a note. It performs no filesystem write in this source. The complete input/output records package graph/ranking/projections, document/project metadata and emitted filename/content strings.",
    "LeanLatexPresentationRule stores an actual input-to-output function and independently chosen respectsRanking:Prop with a supplied proof. It defines no formula linking that proposition to the ranking, graph, emittedFiles or apply fields. The genuine theorem projects the supplied proof under the whole R premise.",
    "Even the input graph and ranking.graph are not required equal. The full context ReferenceRanking does have actual completeness and Pairwise order formulas, but this source does not connect respectsRanking to those formulas. No link is inferred.",
    "The complete presentation/materializer/document schemas are operational artifact metadata; preserve whole exact archives under Math AGENTS rather than materializing maintained workflow schemas or weakening the mixed type. No parser/kernel, Lean elaboration, LaTeX rendering, compiler or IO operation is executed or certified.",
    "All six direct context captures and ReferenceGraph were fully read. Root Document/Rule/LeanProjection/ReferenceRank/ReferenceGraph path hints differ from their Presentation import paths and remain unresolved contextual evidence only."
  ],
